      "side": 1,
      "message": "That value is outside the range of protobuf enums. Per https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#enum:\n\n\"\nEnumerator constants must be in the range of a 32-bit integer. Since enum values use varint encoding on the wire, negative values are inefficient and thus not recommended.\n\"\n\nWould it be possible to use 0 (or 0x7FFFFFFF) for invalid? That would avoid having to write logic to translate between the integer values of this enum and enums in protobufs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 23
      },
